# sweep-mirror-leaks.steps -- what the mirror's reflected pass leaked into
# the view (#517), on tools/mk-mirror-testgame.py's maps/demo1p.bsp: demo1
# with the floor of a pool (rtex241, 44 faces on z = -520, water up to -384)
# renamed to window02_1.  No retail map has a mirror.
#
# R_Mirror (gl_rmain.c) renders the scene again from the view reflected in
# the mirror's plane, through the same R_RenderScene -> R_SetupFrame ->
# R_SetupGL the view took, then blends the mirror's own surfaces over it at
# r_mirroralpha -- drawn from the VIEW.  What the reflected setup derived from
# the reflected view was not put back for them:
#
#   caustics   R_SetupFrame writes the world frame record's caustics from
#              r_viewleaf.  The camera here is in the pool (a CONTENTS_WATER
#              leaf); its reflection, 100 units below the floor, is not.  So
#              the mirror lost the caustics the view puts on it.
#   r_speeds   R_SetupFrame zeroed the poly counters, and the reflected pass
#              threw away the view's: r_speeds 1 on a mirror map counted the
#              reflection and the mirror surfaces only.
#   dlights    R_SetupGL re-clustered the dlights against the reflected view.
#              Not in these frames, because on a mirror whose surfaces all
#              lie on its plane -- every mirror tools/mk-mirror-testgame.py
#              writes -- it has nothing to show: a point on the plane is the
#              same distance from both eyes and lands on the same pixel, so
#              it looks up the same froxel, and a light reaches it in one
#              grid exactly when it does in the other.  A run with a fixed-
#              radius torch (a light_torch_castle with a targetname, as
#              tools/dlight-leak-check.sh adds one) by the floor could not
#              tell the two binaries apart either: a mirror frame is not
#              reproducible run to run (47 - 49 dB GL against GL, the same
#              binary, no entities drawn), only within one run.
#              tools/test_mirror_view_state.py holds the restore.
#
# The frames, from inside the pool looking down at the floor, paused:
#   20-pool               r_mirroralpha 0.5, r_caustics 1
#   21-pool-nocaus        r_caustics 0
#   22-pool-a1            r_mirroralpha 1 (no mirror), r_caustics 1
#   23-pool-a1-nocaus     r_mirroralpha 1, r_caustics 0
#
# THE CHECKS (tools/mirror-leaks-check.sh <dir>), each inside one run:
#   1. Caustics reach the mirror: 20 against 21 changes at least MIN_CAUS
#      pixels.  The view is almost all mirror; before the fix only the
#      pool's walls changed.
#   2. r_speeds 1 counts the view: what r_drawviewmodel 1 adds to epoly is
#      the same with the mirror on as off.  Only R_RenderView draws the view
#      model, so before the fix the reflected pass zeroed it with the mirror
#      on.  (wpoly cannot say it: the reflected pass draws more than the view
#      from every camera tried, before the fix as after.)
#
# Measured 2026-11-22, 800x600, llvmpipe, the pre-fix binary (master at
# "docs(release-notes): r35 notes add the shadow-map unit fix (#528)") and the
# fix, the same basedir:
#
#                          pre-fix                  fix
#   1. caustics            2,333 px   FAIL          133,145 px   OK
#   2. view model epoly    +0 on / +320 off FAIL    +320 / +320  OK
#   wpoly, mirror on       225 (reflection only)    289 (the view's 64 too)
#   wpoly, mirror off      79                       79
#
# Run it on GL, and on the pre-fix binary to see both fail:
#
#   ./tools/mk-mirror-testgame.py $B          # $B holds data1 (see its header)
#   A="-fsaa 0 +gamma 1 -game mirror +map demo1p"
#   STEPS=tools/sweep-mirror-leaks.steps ENGINE=$E ./tools/headless-drive.sh script /tmp/ml $B $A
#   ./tools/mirror-leaks-check.sh /tmp/ml

sleep 20
cmd god
cmd notarget
cmd noclip
cmd viewsize 120
cmd crosshair 0
cmd showpause 0
cmd r_skyspeed_back 0
cmd r_skyspeed_front 0
cmd r_skybox_speed 0
cmd r_flatlightstyles 1
cmd r_dynamic 0
cmd r_gpulightstyles 0
cmd r_ssao 0
cmd r_bloom 0
cmd r_dlight_occlusion 0
cmd r_alias_gpu 0
cmd r_particles 0
cmd gl_texture_anisotropy 1
cmd r_oit 0
cmd r_waterwarp 0
cmd r_softparticles 0
cmd r_softemu 0
cmd r_scale 1
cmd gl_waterwarp_speed 0
cmd r_caustics 1
cmd gl_glows 0
cmd gl_missile_glows 0
cmd gl_other_glows 0
cmd r_drawviewmodel 0
cmd r_drawentities 1
cmd r_drawparticles 0
cmd gl_particles 1
cmd r_wateralpha 0.33
cmd r_lavaalpha 0
cmd r_water_pixel_warp 0
cmd r_skyalpha 1
cmd r_fastsky 0
cmd r_skyfog 0
cmd fog 0
cmd gl_cull 1
cmd r_mirroralpha 0.5
sleep 2

cmd setpos 200 0 -470 80 0 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 20-pool
cmd r_caustics 0
shot 21-pool-nocaus
cmd r_mirroralpha 1
cmd r_caustics 1
shot 22-pool-a1
cmd r_caustics 0
shot 23-pool-a1-nocaus
cmd r_caustics 1

# r_speeds 1, four ways: the mirror on and off, the view model on and off.
cmd r_drawviewmodel 1
cmd r_mirroralpha 0.5
cmd echo REPORT-SPEEDS-MIRROR-VM-BEGIN
cmd r_speeds 1
sleep 1
cmd r_speeds 0
cmd echo REPORT-SPEEDS-MIRROR-VM-END
cmd r_drawviewmodel 0
cmd echo REPORT-SPEEDS-MIRROR-BEGIN
cmd r_speeds 1
sleep 1
cmd r_speeds 0
cmd echo REPORT-SPEEDS-MIRROR-END
cmd r_mirroralpha 1
cmd r_drawviewmodel 1
cmd echo REPORT-SPEEDS-A1-VM-BEGIN
cmd r_speeds 1
sleep 1
cmd r_speeds 0
cmd echo REPORT-SPEEDS-A1-VM-END
cmd r_drawviewmodel 0
cmd echo REPORT-SPEEDS-A1-BEGIN
cmd r_speeds 1
sleep 1
cmd r_speeds 0
cmd echo REPORT-SPEEDS-A1-END
cmd r_mirroralpha 0.5
cmd viewpos
cmd pause
sleep 1
